Luke Skywalker has pretty much always  been at the center of the Star Wars  stories he was the hero whose journey  the entire original trilogy centered on  his birth was the end game of the  prequels and the new film series seems  to focus first on finding him and then  building his relationship with Rey but  in the footage for the last Jedi he  looks much more trouble than usual so  what does it mean that Luke's demeanor  seems so much darker than what we've  seen in the past let's explore some of  the possible consequences for Luke's new  outlook who's the last Jedi writer  director Rian Johnson said point blank  on Twitter that Luke is the last Jedi  mentioned in the title to episode 8 but  filmmakers lie to their audiences all  the time so until the movie hits  theaters it's fair game to speculate if  Luke has begun to journey down a path of  darkness he'd no longer be a Jedi and  the order would be done but perhaps what  Johnson meant is not that Luke is the  last Jedi ever but that he's the last of  the Jedi as we've come to know them  throughout the franchise the Jedi we've  seen so far in the Star Wars movies have  been plagued by politics and war and  have strayed from the Jedi code while  claiming to follow it their arrogance  and blindness led to their virtual  decimation and even Luke's path to  becoming a Jedi in the original trilogy  didn't seem to introduce a true New Jedi  Order so if my episode 8 Luke is turning  away from the teachings of the Jedi  himself then the Jedi as we come to know  them could be over leaving Luke as the  last Jedi of his kind the question is  this will the decline of that particular  type of Jedi happen while a new and  improved order is formed by say Rey it's  a nice idea at the very least is it even  a dark turn the teachings of the Jedi  Order adhere to a strict set of  philosophies that form a stark contrast  with those of the Sith the jedi believe  emotions dictating actions can lead to  the dark side meanwhile the Sith embrace  the full spectrum of emotion good and  bad and as we've seen characters like  ahsoka and the TV shows Clone Wars and  rebels have rejected the Jedi philosophy  without actually going to the dark side  the last Jedi heavily teases a darker  turn for Luke Skywalker but maybe he's  not actually going to the dark side he  could  certainly reject the Sitz teachings -  either way the rogue one debut of the  guardians of the Wills proves that the  force will still live on because it's  not always defined by Jedi Knights and  Sith Lords the force will find other  Guardians even if the Skywalker family  is finished the family name the  Skywalker saga has been a devastating  one Anakin became Darth Vader his  grandson Ben solo became kylo Ren and  now Luke has apparently failed at  passing the way of the Jedi on to the  next generation  for a family with not one but two  potential chosen ones meant to bring  balance to the force that seems like a  pretty lousy track record at some point  we've got to ask ourselves are the  Skywalker's doomed yes the force and  those who use it are always in a state  of flux in balance one minute and out of  it the next but the Skywalker's in  particular seem to have a more  tumultuous relationship with it and each  Skywalker actually seems to ultimately  doom the next Anakin may have saved Luke  but as time as Darth Vader is what  ultimately inspired Ben's solos turned  to darkness and Luke himself failed to  teach Ben the ways of the Jedi allowing  him to be seduced by Snoke and the dark  side if Luke is not in fact the chosen  one and he has turned away from the  light side the Skywalker family may not  receive another chance their story at  least as it relates to being guardians  of the force may well be over unless the  future of Rey Rey is a tremendously  powerful force user and certainly seems  to be on the side of good but she still  might not take up the traditional mantle  of the Jedi while being led to believe  that Rey will be a Jedi master student  it's becoming more clear that may not be  the case Lucas showed teaching Rey how  to Commander powers and how to become  more in touch with the force but that  isn't the same thing as a Jedi Master  training a Padawan learning to better  command the force won't automatically  make her a Jedi with Luke saving to  stray further away from the traditional  teachings of the Jedi Rey could be  exposed to elements of the darkside  during her training her journey through  the forest will be shaped by your  teacher and her teacher definitely seems  to be in a grim place that's not to say  ray will be evil or even that her  learning more about the dark side is a  bad thing  strictly adhering to a philosophy of  pure good and evil as  led to the fall of the Jedi to begin  with rather it seems likely rey is going  to be taught not to suppress and control  her emotions but to let them guide her  when the time is right and they might  even guide her to rescuing Luke himself  Luke from the moment he steps on screen  in the force awakens is clearly in need  of help with Rey's arrival he suddenly  faced the face of the pure-hearted young  force user who could restore his faith  ray thinks she's here to bring Luke back  to save the galaxy but the truth may be  that she's here to save him could she be  the key to restoring the Skywalker  legacy for good and the Jedi to thanks  for watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you'll love to  [Music]
 

